# Node: direct closed calculation; exact complex parts
# Before (rejected by the baseline release):
# re((1+2*i)*(3-i))=5
# Former behavior: JSON success=false and process exit 1.
# Now: the same assertion and its exact eval are supported.
# Boundary: false results and ill-defined inputs still reject; see
# examples/negative/closed_exact_elementary_calculation/.
# Run: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/closed_complex_parts_calculation.lit

re((1+2*i)*(3-i))=5
img((1+2*i)*(3-i))=5
re((1+2*i)/(3-i))=1/10
img((1+2*i)/(3-i))=7/10
re((1/3+i/2)/(1+i))=5/12
img((1/3+i/2)/(1+i))=1/12
re((1+i)^2)=0
img((1+i)^2)=2
re((1+i)^(-1))=1/2
img((1+i)^(-1))=-1/2
1/(1+i)=(1-i)/2
eval re((1+2*i)*(3-i))
eval img((1+2*i)/(3-i))
eval (1+2*i)/(3-i)
eval (1+i)^2
